course: dictionary
lesson: 16123
title: Words for small sounds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To whimper means to make small, weak crying sounds because you are scared, hurt or sad. «The puppy whimpered at the closed door» tells you the puppy was lonely and wanted to get out, even though it was too small to bark loudly.
explain: Whimper can also be a noun, meaning a small, quiet cry: «She let out a whimper when she stubbed her toe.» The word shows the cry was soft, not a loud shriek or a howl.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like «softly», «frightened» or «hurt» point towards whimper. «He tried to be brave, but a tiny whimper escaped» shows a scared boy who is trying to stay quiet.
explain: Use the swap check: put cry into the sentence and ask, was it small and weak? If yes, whimper is the better choice, because it tells you the sound was soft and sad, not loud.
fact: To whimper means to make small, weak crying sounds because you are scared, hurt or sad.
fact: A whimper is a small, quiet cry.
fact: Whimper can be a verb (whimpers, whimpered, whimpering) or a noun (a whimper).
fact: «Without a whimper» means without complaining.
fact: «Not with a bang but a whimper» means ending quietly and weakly, not in a big way.
exercise: «The lost puppy whimpered under the bench.» What does whimpered mean here? | Barked loudly at the postman | *Made small, weak crying sounds | Slept soundly all night | Ran fast across the park
exercise: «She took the bad news without a whimper.» What does without a whimper mean? | Very loudly and angrily | *Without complaining | Without any clothes on | Without a voice, because she was ill
exercise: «Tom gave a tiny whimper when he fell.» Find and copy the word that is a noun for a small, quiet cry. | *whimper | tiny | gave | fell
test: What does whimper mean? | Run away very fast | *Make small, weak crying sounds | Shout angrily at someone | Laugh loudly at a joke
test: «The team lost the game, not with a bang but a whimper.» What does this phrase suggest? | The game ended with fireworks and cheering | The team won in the last second | The crowd started a loud song | *The game ended quietly and weakly
exam: Which sentence uses whimper as a noun, meaning a small, quiet cry? | *«She let out a whimper.» | «He ran fast to school.» | «They whimpered all night.»
